Authorization

Enforce identity, role, ownership, organization status and resource permissions in backend handlers. Configure Firestore Security Rules for direct client access. Remember that privileged server SDK operations bypass Firestore Security Rules and therefore require independent authorization checks.

Protect against forged roles, modified request bodies, insecure direct object references, privilege escalation and unauthorized access through direct URLs or API calls.

Add rate limiting to sensitive operations where appropriate, safe error messages, access revocation and audit events for administrative actions.

