Safety eligibility

Implement configurable food-safety eligibility rules reviewed against applicable Indian requirements. Consider food type, preparation time, storage conditions, transport conditions, known contamination and the declared collection deadline.

Do not claim that a donor declaration or an automated algorithm certifies food as safe. Use explicit states such as PENDING_REVIEW, ELIGIBLE_FOR_MATCHING and SAFETY_HOLD.

Prevent expired, reported unsafe or ineligible food from being matched. Create an incident workflow to suspend affected donations and record review and resolution events.

Lifecycle

Implement validated transitions between:
DRAFT, PENDING_REVIEW, AVAILABLE, RESERVED, ACCEPTED, PICKUP_ASSIGNED, COLLECTED and DELIVERED.

Also support REJECTED, EXPIRED, CANCELLED and appropriate exception states such as FAILED_PICKUP and SAFETY_HOLD.

Do not permit arbitrary state changes. Use server-side validation and transactions where needed.

Quantity integrity

Track total quantity, reserved quantity, collected quantity, delivered quantity and remaining available quantity using explicit units.

Prevent overselling, duplicate reservations and invalid delivery quantities. Support partial allocation and partial delivery if implemented, with documented rules.

Make retried operations safe and prevent duplicate events.

Donor features

Implement create, edit, draft, publish, cancel, list, filter and history operations. Allow editing only when permitted by the current lifecycle state.

Persist every successful change and return accurate error responses when an operation fails.

Verification

Test valid and invalid submissions, deadlines, safety holds, concurrent acceptance, quantity limits, cancellations, partial allocations and persistence after refresh.

Use actual database records throughout. Do not use mock responses as proof of functionality.
Continue the AnnaSetu codebase and implement the recipient matching engine and reservation APIs.

Eligibility

Consider only verified recipients and currently available donations that have passed configured eligibility checks, have not expired and are not on safety hold.

Evaluate:

* Geographic distance and service area.
* Food category and dietary requirements.
* Known allergens and restrictions.
* Quantity and meal-serving capacity.
* Pickup hours and availability.
* Transport capacity.
* Collection deadline and estimated travel feasibility.
* Current workload and outstanding reservations.

Hard eligibility constraints must take priority over ranking scores. Never match food to an incompatible recipient simply because it is nearby.

Matching algorithm

Implement a documented, deterministic ranking function with configurable weights for distance, urgency, capacity, compatibility and pickup feasibility.

Use actual stored coordinates and actual routing results when available. Label straight-line distance as such when road-routing data is unavailable.

Explain the ranking factors for each suggested match. Do not use generative AI guesses for safety eligibility, coordinates or organization verification.

Reservation

Implement authenticated acceptance and decline operations.

Before accepting, recheck eligibility, remaining quantity, expiry, recipient capacity and current reservation state. Use Firestore transactions or equivalent concurrency-safe logic so concurrent requests cannot reserve the same quantity.

Implement a server-enforced reservation expiration mechanism using a supported scheduled backend process, or an equally reliable server-side expiry mechanism. Release expired reservations safely and idempotently.

Prevent duplicate acceptance, conflicting reservations and invalid state transitions.

Recipient operations

Implement eligible-offer discovery, search, filters, donation details, acceptance, decline, accepted donations, pickup history and recipient capacity settings.

Return real results with pagination and appropriate empty states.

Tests

Test incompatible food, zero remaining quantity, expired donations, safety holds, unverified recipients, insufficient capacity, concurrent acceptance and reservation expiry.

Report test results and fix failures before proceeding.
