Maps integration

Integrate Google Maps Platform using the required supported APIs:

* Maps JavaScript API.
* Places API for address search.
* Geocoding API where needed.
* Routes API for road routes and travel estimates.

Request only necessary permissions. Keep server credentials private and restrict browser keys to approved origins and APIs. Ask me to configure missing credentials and billing rather than inventing routes or locations.

India-only validation

Validate addresses and coordinates on the backend using trusted geocoding results and country identifiers. Support Indian states, union territories, cities, districts and PIN codes.

Reject out-of-country donation origins, recipient destinations, pickup addresses and delivery destinations. Validate the address and its coordinates together. Do not silently substitute an invalid address with a nearby location.

Use real GPS readings only when a user grants browser permission. Provide manual address entry if permission is denied.

Location privacy

Request location access after a clear user action. Show location permission status, timestamp of the last update and available accuracy information.

Do not silently track users or claim continuous tracking when only a single position is available. Limit collection, access and retention of volunteer location data.

Only authorized participants may access operational pickup locations.

Pickup and delivery workflow

Implement validated pickup events such as:
ASSIGNED, EN_ROUTE_TO_PICKUP, ARRIVED_AT_PICKUP, COLLECTED, EN_ROUTE_TO_RECIPIENT, ARRIVED_AT_RECIPIENT and DELIVERED.

Include documented cancellation, delay, rejection and failed-pickup paths.

Store each event with server timestamp, actor, pickup ID and relevant details. Do not permit unauthorized users to skip required transitions.

Delivery confirmation

At collection, record an authorized handover and collected quantity. At delivery, require recipient confirmation or a securely generated, expiring, single-use handover code.

Validate codes on the backend with retry limits and duplicate-submission protection. Record delivered quantity, rejected quantity and discrepancies.

GPS proximity is supporting evidence, not proof of delivery.

Failure handling

Handle denied GPS permission, stale positions, unavailable maps, invalid addresses, missing credentials and routing failures without breaking other application functions.

Never fabricate coordinates, live locations or ETAs.

Tests

Test valid Indian addresses, out-of-country destinations, GPS denial, stale locations, route failures, unauthorized tracking, invalid state transitions, duplicate codes and partial deliveries.
